in the following video i will show you  how quickly and simply you can analyze  your data directly online with data tab  in order to do this go to datadeb.net  and click on the online statistics  calculator  then click on clear table and insert  your own data into the table  i will now use the example data once you  entered your data  the variables that you want to analyze  appear here below  it is important to make sure that the  names of your variables  appear in the first row in these steps  you will find the methods you need to  analyze your data  in the first step you can analyze your  data descriptively  for example you can display the mean  value  or the standard deviation you can also  create  frequency tables and crosstabs  in the next step you can perform a  variety of hypotheses tests  tata dab always helps you to find the  right test  an example in your survey you ask men  and women about their salary  now you want to know whether men and  women differ in terms of salary  in order to find it out you select the  variables  salary and gender now data tab tells you  which test is suitable for your question  and suggests  the t-test for independent samples if  the conditions for the independent  t-tests are not  met you can calculate a non-parametric  test  the mann-whitney u test of course you  can also calculate  many other hypotheses tests with data  tab  for example if you click on a nominal  variable with more than two values  an analysis of variance is automatically  performed  so this means data tab always suggests  the appropriate test  depending on which variables you select  what other methods are available in  datadeb.net  of course you can also easily calculate  a correlation  analysis a regression analysis  a principal component analysis and a  cluster analysis  so this was a first overview of the  possibilities of data tab  you can find more detailed information  about the statistical methods in our  tutorials  or you can take a look at our youtube  channel  thanks for listening
 

